# Regenerate the three locks with Python 3.12 and pip-tools:
#   pip-compile --generate-hashes --allow-unsafe -o requirements.lock requirements.in
#   pip-compile --generate-hashes --allow-unsafe -o requirements-build.lock requirements-build.in
#   pip-compile --generate-hashes --allow-unsafe -o requirements-brief.lock requirements-brief.in
#
# Packages for the jobs that hold no secret: scripts/fetch_and_build.py, the
# learning candidates (scripts/learn/candidates.py) and the slides
# (scripts/learn/render.py, which uses python-pptx). scripts/send_email.py uses
# only the Python standard library and needs nothing from this file. The one
# job that holds the Anthropic key installs requirements-brief.lock instead.
#
# The workflow installs requirements.lock, which pins every package, including
# the transitive ones, to an exact version and sha256 hash. sgmllib3k comes only
# as an sdist, so its build backend (setuptools) is pinned the same way in
# requirements-build.lock and installed first. After editing this file,
# regenerate the locks with the lines above (pip install pip-tools first) and
# install them with:
#   pip install --require-hashes -r requirements-build.lock
#   pip install --require-hashes --no-build-isolation -r requirements.lock
